# Siraj Portfolio — Cursor Rules

Read CLAUDE.md and README.md for the full architecture and workflow.

## Stack and files
- Preserve Astro, Tailwind CSS v4 through its Vite plugin, TypeScript, native HTML dialogs, and lightweight CSS 3D transforms.
- Use focused `.astro` components in `src/components/` and keep the document in `src/pages/index.astro`.
- Keep personal content and section definitions in `src/config.ts`.
- Keep interaction behavior in `src/scripts/portfolio.ts` and styles in `src/styles/global.css`. Custom CSS is appropriate for perspective, transforms, dialog transitions, and responsive layouts; Tailwind utilities are also available.
- Use the existing SVG line-icon component and maintain the readable monospace, black-and-violet aesthetic.

## Content and behavior
- Keep the six sections: introduction, about, achievements, projects, learning, and contact. Match section IDs, dialog IDs, and interaction data attributes.
- Closed cards show only a title and matching icon. All section prose and empty states appear inside activated dialogs.
- Projects and achievements use typed entries with `title`, `description`, optional `url`, and optional `tags`. Empty arrays show “Coming soon” inside their dialogs.
- Do not fabricate personal claims, qualifications, projects, social accounts, or a portrait. Do not add a certificates section.
- Keep carousel rotation visitor-controlled. Preserve dragging, swiping, buttons, indicators, keyboard controls, and drag-versus-click handling without interfering with vertical scrolling.
- Preserve dialog labels, close buttons, Escape behavior, focus management/restoration, internal scrolling, and paused background interaction.
- Keep the compact section menu, mobile layout, reduced-motion static grid, visible focus states, and protection against horizontal page overflow.

## Verification and deployment
Use Node.js 24.12 or newer in the Node 24 LTS line.

```sh
npm ci
npm run dev
npm run check
npm test
npm run build
npm run preview
```

`npm test` rebuilds the HTML fixture and runs happy-dom interaction tests. DOM tests do not verify browser rendering, native modal focus trapping, real touch input, or visual overflow. Perform browser checks when available and report verification limits accurately.

Production output is static `dist/`. Set `PUBLIC_SITE_URL` to the final HTTPS URL, including its trailing slash and any deployment subpath, before building for production. Preserve base-path-aware links, the PNG social image, and SVG favicon. Publishing is a separate action.

Preserve LICENSE.md, including the original MIT licence and Ryan Fitzgerald’s copyright notice.
